# Build output. Prettier walks the whole tree, and cargo leaves tens of
# thousands of JSON files under target/ that are nobody's to format.
out/
release/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# Generated from the TypeScript and compared byte for byte against it. Letting
# a formatter reshape one of these would be a fixture changing to meet a tool.
conformance/

# The same argument. These are deliberately awkward markdown — a file with no
# body, one that opens with a byte-order mark, one that ends every tag block a
# different way — and the seeder writes them so the parser can be caught
# mishandling them. Formatting them would quietly rewrite the question.
scripts/seed/vault/

pnpm-lock.yaml

# Drizzle's own output: the migrations and the snapshots it diffs them against.
# Reformatting a snapshot would change the thing the next `generate` compares
# to, which is the fixture argument again in a different coat.
drizzle/

# Astro's own output and caches.
out/web/
.astro/
